WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.340
The Lost Ship by Stephen Colbourn.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.400
Sunday, 5th December, 1872.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.293
The weather is fine.

00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:30.996
The wind is blowing and the ship is sailing quickly.

00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:33.268
The men are happy.

00:00:33.328 --> 00:00:37.520
We are sailing between Cuba and Florida.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.662
We are going to be in Florida soon.

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:48.156
We are going to reach Florida in three or four days.

00:00:48.216 --> 00:00:53.648
This is the Captain of the ship.

00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:56.510
He is in his cabin.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.694
He is writing in the ship's log book.

00:01:00.754 --> 00:01:05.738
The Captain writes in the log book every day.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:11.582
He writes about the weather and he writes about the ship.

00:01:11.642 --> 00:01:16.345
He also writes about the men on the ship.

00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:19.736
The ship is old.

00:01:19.796 --> 00:01:22.668
It is a sailing ship.

00:01:22.728 --> 00:01:27.720
The wind blows and the ship sails.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.666
The Captain and his men are going home.

00:01:32.726 --> 00:01:36.526
They are going to reach home soon.

00:01:36.586 --> 00:01:40.537
They are well and happy.

00:01:40.597 --> 00:01:45.598
Captain! There's a strange ship near us.

00:01:45.658 --> 00:01:50.808
Can you come on deck?

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:58.511
Now the Captain and all the men are on deck.

00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:02.184
They are looking at the strange ship.

00:02:02.244 --> 00:02:05.676
It's a very strange ship.

00:02:05.736 --> 00:02:08.468
There's no name on the ship.

00:02:08.529 --> 00:02:11.330
There are no men on deck.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.212
Where are the ship's men?

00:02:14.272 --> 00:02:17.064
The Captain is shouting.

00:02:17.124 --> 00:02:18.696
Hallo!

00:02:18.755 --> 00:02:21.146
Is anybody there?

00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:23.639
Can you hear me?

00:02:23.698 --> 00:02:26.564
Is anybody there?

00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:31.558
But there is no answer from the strange ship.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.780
Where are the men on the ship?

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.222
Are they ill?

00:02:39.282 --> 00:02:45.654
The Captain gets into a small boat.

00:02:45.714 --> 00:02:49.636
Two men go in the boat with him.

00:02:49.696 --> 00:02:54.178
They row across to the strange ship.

00:02:54.237 --> 00:02:59.418
They are going to look for the men on the ship.

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:04.949
The Captain is on the deck of the strange ship.

00:03:05.009 --> 00:03:08.390
The two men are with him.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.770
They walk along the deck.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.721
They go to the ship's wheel.

00:03:15.781 --> 00:03:19.592
There is nobody at the wheel.

00:03:19.652 --> 00:03:23.580
Nobody is steering the ship.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.428
The ship is sailing in the wind.

00:03:27.488 --> 00:03:31.570
The wind is steering the ship.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:37.604
The Captain shouts, Is anybody here?

00:03:37.664 --> 00:03:40.636
There is no answer.

00:03:40.696 --> 00:03:46.378
There is nobody on deck.

00:03:46.438 --> 00:03:52.397
The Captain is below deck.

00:03:52.457 --> 00:03:55.654
He is looking for the ship's men.

00:03:55.714 --> 00:03:59.376
He cannot find them.

00:03:59.436 --> 00:04:04.378
Now he is in the cabin where the men eat.

00:04:04.438 --> 00:04:07.050
There is a table.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:10.532
There is food on the table.

00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:14.604
But who is going to eat the food?

00:04:14.664 --> 00:04:17.936
There is water in the jug.

00:04:17.996 --> 00:04:21.989
But who is going to drink the water?

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:26.162
There is a cigar in the ashtray.

00:04:26.222 --> 00:04:31.485
But who is smoking the cigar?

00:04:31.545 --> 00:04:36.068
This is the Captain's cabin.

00:04:36.128 --> 00:04:39.549
But the Captain is not here.

00:04:39.609 --> 00:04:43.290
There is nobody in the cabin.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.482
There is a table and a chair.

00:04:47.542 --> 00:04:53.225
The ship's log book and a photograph are on the table.

00:04:53.285 --> 00:04:57.887
The ship's log book is open.

00:04:57.947 --> 00:05:04.580
Thursday, 25th November, 1869.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.892
Where are we?

00:05:06.952 --> 00:05:10.203
Somewhere in the Atlantic Ocean?

00:05:10.263 --> 00:05:14.536
Somewhere between Bermuda and Florida?

00:05:14.596 --> 00:05:16.826
I don't know.

00:05:16.886 --> 00:05:20.874
The ship is in a thick white mist.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:25.222
I cannot see the sun or stars.

00:05:25.282 --> 00:05:27.954
There is no wind.

00:05:28.014 --> 00:05:31.386
The ship is not moving.

00:05:31.446 --> 00:05:35.690
Every day I pray for wind.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:39.112
When will the wind come?

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:42.154
The men are angry.

00:05:42.214 --> 00:05:45.286
They want to leave the ship.

00:05:45.346 --> 00:05:48.945
They want to take the small boat.

00:05:49.005 --> 00:05:52.693
They want to row to Florida.

00:05:52.753 --> 00:05:56.214
They want to go home.

00:05:56.274 --> 00:06:02.376
Friday, 26th November, 1869.

00:06:02.436 --> 00:06:05.987
The men are getting into the small boat.

00:06:06.047 --> 00:06:09.458
They are going to row to Florida.

00:06:09.518 --> 00:06:15.396
Saturday, 27th November, 1869.
 
00:06:15.456 --> 00:06:21.086
I am alone. I am waiting for the wind.

00:06:21.145 --> 00:06:24.686
The Captain reads the log book.

00:06:24.746 --> 00:06:28.058
He sees the photograph on the table.

00:06:28.118 --> 00:06:30.169
He picks it up.

00:06:30.229 --> 00:06:33.020
He looks at the photograph.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:39.944
No! No! It can't be!
 
00:06:40.004 --> 00:06:45.426
The Captain looks at the photograph.

00:06:45.486 --> 00:06:48.956
It is a photograph of a man.

00:06:49.016 --> 00:06:53.788
The Captain looks in the mirror on the cabin wall.

00:06:53.847 --> 00:06:57.340
He looks at his face in the mirror.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.454
He looks at the face in the photograph.

00:07:01.514 --> 00:07:04.566
They are the same.

00:07:04.626 --> 00:07:09.941
It is a photograph of himself!

00:07:10.001 --> 00:07:14.955
The Captain runs up on deck.

00:07:15.015 --> 00:07:19.352
There is a thick white mist around the ship.

00:07:19.412 --> 00:07:22.367
The Captain looks around.

00:07:22.426 --> 00:07:25.088
He can see nobody.

00:07:25.148 --> 00:07:28.041
He can see nothing.

00:07:28.101 --> 00:07:30.984
Where is his ship?

00:07:31.044 --> 00:07:33.736
Where are his men?

00:07:33.796 --> 00:07:36.928
He cannot see the sun.

00:07:36.988 --> 00:07:40.040
He is alone.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.773
I do not know the date.

00:07:43.833 --> 00:07:45.994
Where am I?

00:07:46.054 --> 00:07:48.567
I do not know.

00:07:48.627 --> 00:07:51.898
I am the Captain of this ship.

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:54.819
I must sail the ship.

00:07:54.879 --> 00:07:57.620
Where am I going?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.050
I do not know.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.581
What is my name?

00:08:02.641 --> 00:08:05.982
What is the name of this ship?

00:08:06.042 --> 00:08:08.892
I do not know.

00:08:08.952 --> 00:08:11.512
I am waiting.

00:08:11.572 --> 00:08:15.013
Another ship is going to come.

00:08:15.073 --> 00:08:19.332
Another Captain is going to take my place.

00:08:19.392 --> 00:08:22.704
Then I can rest.

00:08:22.764 --> 00:08:43.000
I am waiting.